  "Number": 23,
  "Question": "If, in the expression \\(x^2-3,\\) \\(x\\) increases or decreases by a positive amount \\(a,\\) the expression changes by an amount:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\pm2ax+a^2\\)",
    "B": "\\(2ax\\pm a^2\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\pm a^2-3\\)",
    "D": "\\((x+a)^2-3\\)",
    "E": "\\((x-a)^2-3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The change is the new value minus the original value; the constant \\(-3\\) therefore cancels.\n\nIf \\(x\\) increases by \\(a>0\\), the change is\n\\[\n\\bigl((x+a)^2-3\\bigr)-(x^2-3)\n=2ax+a^2.\n\\]\nIf \\(x\\) decreases by \\(a\\), the change is\n\\[\n\\bigl((x-a)^2-3\\bigr)-(x^2-3)\n=-2ax+a^2.\n\\]\nTogether these signed changes are \\(\\pm2ax+a^2\\), with the plus sign for increasing \\(x\\) and the minus sign for decreasing \\(x\\). The answer is choice A.",
